{"kind":"assert","text":"P1f export packaging correction stays within scope: commit to the recomputed inventory without enlarging limits; define locale-independent ordering for the new digest.","body":{"all":"The builder reported that the complete P1f evidence fits the existing file and retained-byte limits, but repeating its inventory inline creates a 1,927,507-byte export.json exceeding the unchanged 1 MiB metadata limit. I inspected the current compact @2 implementation at 9832d320a97cc83517d30a289b5d7637539c390a: it computes the bounded actual inventory, checks digest/count/bytes, and later requires equality with the full verified closure and its signed manifest digest. This focused correction is within #1082's allowed evidence types/validator/IO scope, with no resource-cap or confidentiality change. Preserve all @1 archived vectors, exact root/path/case checks and old failures, and obtain fresh source-bound verification and independent review including actual @2 positive/negative composition and the complete current evidence envelope.\n\nOne concrete correction is needed before freezing the @2 digest contract: inventoryCommitment currently sorts with localeCompare. I reproduced different orders for the permitted ASCII paths docs/I.txt and docs/i.txt with the same Node executable using English versus Turkish Intl.Collator; locale is not part of the signed inventory schema. Define a deterministic ASCII/code-unit ordering for this new commitment, independent of process locale and insertion order, and test it. Preserve historical @1 digest/vector behavior rather than silently rewriting old evidence. This is a fail-closed portability/canonicalization issue, not evidence of an approval bypass. No real adoption, operational gate success or downstream phase is authorized by this observation."}}